---
import UtilityLayout from "../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Privacy & operating limits"
  description="What UtilityPot sends to Jev, what stays in your browser, and how public-page fetching and inference are bounded."
  slug=""
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Utilities that stay in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      CSV/JSON conversion, date cleanup and meeting-time calculation run in your
      browser without AI. Diagram rendering is also local after its source steps
      and connections have been interpreted by AI. This application has no
      account database, saved input history, session replay or input analytics.
      Anonymous, opt-out-respecting PostHog analytics measure page views and
      coarse tool actions, using a pseudonymous browser identifier in local
      storage rather than analytics cookies. SDK opt-out is stored in the
      browser. Pageview URLs retain the public path but remove query strings and
      fragments; referrers are reduced to their origin, and campaign/ad-click
      identifiers are discarded, including persisted acquisition properties.
      Analytics does not record form values, page text, provider responses, or
      output. Family and creator discovery clicks record only a fixed
      destination name and placement (intro, result or project showcase), not
      link text or input. These clicks do not establish return visits. Local
      computation and downloads remain in your browser; download events measure
      user intent, not completed transfer. Hosting providers still process
      ordinary request metadata under their own policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Utilities that use AI</h2>
    <p>
      Entity extraction, flowchart interpretation and webpage evidence selection
      use AI. After explicit consent, the context described beside the primary
      action is sent to our Cloudflare Worker and TypeSafe. This can include
      source text, category definitions, step relationships or questions. Do not
      submit confidential or personal information without authority. The
      application does not persist these inputs or log provider bodies. TypeSafe
      processing and retention are governed by its terms, not a claim that
      inference is fully local.
    </p>
    <h2>Public-page reading</h2>
    <p>
      Reading a public page sends its URL to our server. Cloudflare resolves the
      public hostname and fetches HTTP/HTTPS pages through its public Internet
      network boundary; URL and DNS checks repeat on every redirect. The
      destination receives the requested URL, and Cloudflare DNS receives the
      hostname. No browser cookies, authorization or provider secrets are
      forwarded. The reader executes no scripts or embedded requests, accepts
      only UTF-8 HTML/plain text, and caps reading at 250,000 bytes, eight
      seconds and three redirects. Only 10,000 characters / 100 paragraphs are
      searched, with truncation disclosed. Blocked, authenticated,
      JavaScript-only or unsupported pages can be used by pasting text. This is
      not a paywall bypass.
    </p>
    <h2>Secrets and spending</h2>
    <p>
      TYPESAFE_API_KEY is a server-side Worker secret. The browser never
      receives it. Requests are limited to 16 KB and a bounded set of
      server-authored questions. Each provider request has a 15-second timeout;
      an entity section has a 30-second total deadline. Documents up to 2 MiB
      run in complete-source sections, paced to respect the existing request
      limits. A failed section rejects the whole result; there are no automatic
      retries. Client and aggregate limits are 6 and 30 requests per minute per
      Cloudflare location. These limits are eventually consistent and are not a
      strict global billing cap. Provider-side spend limits are required before
      public AI launch.
    </p>
    <h2>Output boundaries</h2>
    <p>
      Typed choices and confidence do not guarantee correctness. Review results.
      Entity extraction can miss or mislabel mentions despite processing every
      section. Source excerpts are not independent fact verification. Missing
      credentials, protection or valid output produce an explicit failure, not
      fake model results.
    </p>
  </section>
</UtilityLayout>
